<title>INDIA: HOCKEY-WOMEN'S INDIRA GANDHI GOLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-WOMEN'S INDIRA GANDHI GOLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the Indira Gandhi</p>
<p>Gold Cup women's hockey tournament on Saturday:</p>
<p>South Korea beat Australia 2-1 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>South Korea - Jang Jung-eun (26), Choi Mi-soon (53)</p>
<p>Australia - Kelly Free (4)</p>
<p>China beat Russia 8-1 (halftime 6-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>China - Jang Hiu Yan (16, 29, 58, 66), Huang Jun</p>
<p>Xia (25), Liu Yang (28, 32), Yang Hui Ping (35)</p>
<p>Russia - V.Tatyana (53)</p>
<p>    Final group standings  Pl  W   D   L   F    A   Pts</p>
<p> South Korea		   4   4   0   0   18   4   12</p>
<p> Australia		     4   2   0   2   18   8    6</p>
<p> India			   4   2   0   2   10   5    6</p>
<p> China			   4   2   0   2   14  11    6</p>
<p> Russia			  4   0   0   4    2  34    0</p>
<p>NOTE: South Korea meet Australia in the final on Sunday and</p>
<p>India play China for third place.</p>
</text>
